我以前在博斯科姆当
采访过一个哥们儿，
是个战斗机飞行员。
I once went to interview
a fighter pilot. Bloke I had
met down in Boscombe Down.

538
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:49,440
他是个教官，
专门培训战斗机飞行员的人。
He was a trainer.
Bloke who trained
fighter pilots.

539
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:51,040
结果他开一辆米黄色的沃尔沃。
He had a beige Volvo.

540
00:27:51,080 --> 00:27:52,480
希尔：对。
HILL: Yeah.

541
00:27:52,520 --> 00:27:53,960
为什么你们这帮人，
明明平日里体验过
Why do you all,
when you've lived

542
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,880
时速300英里的极速，
私底下却开破烂呢？
at 300 miles an hour,
drive rubbish?

543
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:58,720
正因为我们体验过
时速300英里的极速啊。
Because we've lived
at 300 miles an hour.

544
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,920
所以日常就根本不需要……
So you don't need
the actual...

545
00:28:00,960 --> 00:28:02,880
你只想要辆实用的车，
能把你带到目的地就行。
What you just want
is something practical
that gets you around.

546
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:06,440
你不再需要所谓的驾驶快感了，
毕竟你早就爽够了。
You don't need the thrill,
if you like, of driving.
You've had that.

547
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,440
怎么，所以你现在就开着奥迪
到处慢吞吞地瞎晃悠？
What, so you just
pootle around now
in your Audi?

548
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:11,640
倒也不算慢吞吞瞎晃，
但你也知道……
I don't exactly pootle,
but you know...

549
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:15,240
路上有太多人
开着车身巨宽的福特GT招摇过市了。
There's too many people
driving very wide Ford GTs.

550
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:17,320
-[观众大笑]
-还是左舵的。
-[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
-And left-hand drives.

551
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:20,400
开福特GT的男人
可慢不下来，因为……
The slowest men
are not driving Ford GTs,
because it's...

552
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,840
得，又扯回福特了。
Again, back with Ford.

553
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:25,520
难道你就不怀念那种
飙到起飞的刺激感吗？
Don't you miss the excitement
of going a million?

554
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:27,640
不过这事还有个必然代价。
Well, there's
a corollary to that.

555
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:32,040
那就是你随时可能面临
致命的车祸。
There's the imminent accident
that you can experience.

556
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:34,240
那种罪我真是
受够了，说真的。
And I've had
enough of that, really.

557
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:36,840
我一直赛车开到了39岁。
I raced up to the age of 39.

558
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:40,680
我觉得从生理机制上说，
人总会走到一个节点，
And I think, biologically,
we kind of get to the point

559
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:43,360
脑海深处有个声音在提醒你：
where a little voice
at the back of the head says,

560
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:45,120
“其实，你是有机会
活到60岁的……”
"You know, you could
make it to 60

561
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:47,400
“前提是你真的保养得当，
运气也足够好。”
"if you really
took care of yourself,
if you're lucky."

562
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:50,160
我得承认，这就是为什么
我再也不去玩什么战斗机了。
I must confess, this is why
I don't do the fighter jet
stuff anymore.

563
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:51,400
我只要看着孩子们就会想：
I just look at the kids
and think,

564
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:53,320
“我现在干嘛还要去空中
玩倒栽葱呢？”
"Why do I want to go
upside down now?"

565
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:55,280
我已经玩够了，
再也不想碰了。
I had enough of it.
I don't need any more.

566
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:57,360
-深表同感。
-是啊。
-No, I sympathise with you.
-Yeah.

567
00:28:57,400 --> 00:29:00,720
好了，言归正传，
我们现在得聊聊
你跑的那一圈了。
Okay, right.
We've got to talk now
about your lap.

568
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:03,760
-嗯，好吧。
-[观众轻笑]
-Uh-huh. Yes.
-[AUDIENCE CHUCKLING]

569
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:07,000
那绝对算不上我这辈子
跑得最干净利落的一圈。
It wasn't exactly
my neatest lap
I've ever done in my life.

570
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:09,040
但开那种车确实挺难跑的。
But it's quite difficult
in one of those cars.

571
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:10,760
我可不是在找借口怪车子不行啊，杰里米。
I'm not complaining
about the equipment, Jeremy.

572
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:14,360
那当然不是。
要那样的话……
那可就太有失风度了。
Of course not.
That would be...
That would be poor form.

573
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:17,440
你上一次参加正式比赛
是什么时候？
When was the last time
you drove competitively?

574
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:20,960
我想还是我开F1那会儿吧。
I think when
I was in Formula One.

575
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,240
那么，有谁想看看他这场
名义上的“复出之战”跑得如何吗？
Well, who'd like to see
how he got on then
basically in his comeback?

576
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:25,840
-[观众欢呼]
-[听不清]
-[AUDIENCE CHEERING]
-[INAUDIBLE]

577
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:27,760
放录像！
Play the tape.

578
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:29,600
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TIRES SQUEALING]

579
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:32,240
-克拉克森：
起步烂透了！
-希尔：得了吧。
-CLARKSON:
That's a rubbish start!
-HILL: Oh, come on.

580
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:34,520
这车显然比F1慢太多了，
It's obviously a lot slower
than a Formula One car,

581
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:38,280
但我还是隐约找回了一点
当年肾上腺素飙升的感觉，对。
but I'm still feeling
a little bit of
the old adrenaline, yeah.

582
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:43,280
克拉克森：这走线
可够新鲜的。
CLARKSON: That's
a new line in there.

583
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:46,280
斯提格其实跟我说了，
我那个弯跑得
大错特错。
The Stig actually told me
I was doing it
all wrong there.

584
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:48,480
克拉克森：
呃，我倒觉得……
看着还挺快的。
CLARKSON:
Well, I suspect that...
That looks quite quick.

585
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:50,480
不，我简直就像把怎么开赛车给忘光了。
No, it's almost like I've
forgotten how to do this.

586
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:54,960
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TIRES SQUEALING]

587
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:58,040
-希尔：那个弯过得还行。
-克拉克森：不，那简直
相当漂亮。
-HILL: That was not bad.
-CLARKSON: No, that was
really very good.

588
00:29:58,080 --> 00:30:00,680
-希尔：都切到路肩极限了。
-[克拉克森大笑]
-HILL: Right up to the edge.
-[CLARKSON LAUGHING]

589
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:03,360
-克拉克森：
进锤头弯了！
-[轮胎刺耳摩擦声]
-CLARKSON:
It's the Hammerhead!
-[TIRES SCREECHING]

590
00:30:05,960 --> 00:30:10,000
-哎哟，那一下有点晃！
-啊，稍微压了点线。
-Ooh, a bit wobbly there!
-Ah, just went over the line.

591
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:13,120
我刚才撞死了一只虫子。
I just killed a bug.

592
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:15,640
克拉克森：这个弯我都懒得问你
松没松油门了。
CLARKSON: I'm not even
going to ask you if you
lifted off for this one.

593
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:18,760
-因为你绝不可能松。
-希尔：那是全油门。
-Because there's no way.
-HILL: That was flat.

594
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:20,240
克拉克森：对，
看着确实是地板油。
CLARKSON: Yeah,
looks pretty flat.

595
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,360
希尔：那个弯
很容易全油门过。
HILL: Quite
easily flat, that one.

596
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:24,880
克拉克森：来了，倒数第二个弯，
大多数人都在这儿阴沟翻船。
CLARKSON: Here we go,
second to last corner,
catches most people out.

597
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:28,160
至于你，你也跟大多数人一样啃草去了，然后……
And you, you're on the grass,
like most people, and then...

598
00:30:29,040 --> 00:30:31,040
冲线！
Across the line!

599
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:45,400
那么，你觉得你这次
能排第几？
So where do you think
you've come here, then?

600
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:47,400
呃……
Um...

601
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:49,840
其实我都不敢想。
恐怕会是
个不小的打击。
I dread to think, actually.
It's gonna be
a bit of a shock.

602
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,520
得了吧，快告诉我。
Come on. Tell me.

603
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:53,480
他今儿早上其实还放话呢，
He actually said this morning,

604
00:30:53,520 --> 00:30:55,280
[阴阳怪气地模仿]
“哎呀，要是我没登顶，
我干脆去寻死算了！”
[MOCKINGLY]
"Well, if I'm not at the top,
I'm going to be suicidal!"

605
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:57,560
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

606
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:59,680
你跑出来的成绩是……
You did it.

607
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:04,520
D·希尔。1分
50秒3。
D. Hill. One minute,
50.3 seconds.

608
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:05,760
[懊恼呻吟]
[GROANING]

609
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:10,040
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

610
00:31:10,080 --> 00:31:12,640
他居然当真了！
He actually believed me!

611
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,000
他真上当了！
He fell for it!

612
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:17,120
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

613
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:19,480
噢，我就喜欢看这出！
Oh, I love that so much!

614
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:23,840
你真正的成绩是
1分……
You actually did it
in one minute,

615
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:27,080
46秒3！
女士们先生们！
46.3 seconds,
ladies and gentlemen!

616
00:31:27,120 --> 00:31:28,960
-史上最快！
-[观众吹口哨并欢呼]
-Fastest ever!
-[AUDIENCE WHISTLING
AND CHEERING]

617
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:31,680
有史以来最快！
Fastest ever!

618
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:34,280
一路往上，把吉米·卡尔、
Right up, Jimmy Carr,

619
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:36,520
西蒙·考威尔、
Simon Cowell,

620
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:38,480
茱蒂·洁德、
Jodie Kidd,

621
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:41,600
还有罗尼·奥沙利文，
全都秒成渣了！
Ronnie O'Sullivan,
blown away.

622
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:44,040
不过我也理应跑更快。
毕竟，
我是说要跑不过就搞笑了。
I really ought to, though.
I wouldn't mind,
really, I mean.

623
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:46,440
话是这么说，但我得问问你，
Yeah, but this...
I have to ask you,

624
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:47,880
你是不是觉得这开起来太小儿科了？
did you just find it
incredibly easy?

625
00:31:47,920 --> 00:31:50,480
因为你一路上都在闲聊呢，甚至都没……
'Cause you were chatting
round there. Not even...

626
00:31:50,520 --> 00:31:53,480
是啊，我觉得挺轻松的，
那种铃木小车。
Yeah, I think it's quite easy,
one of those Suzukis.

627
00:31:53,520 --> 00:31:55,600
有大把时间可以琢磨事儿。
There's quite a lot
of time to think.

628
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:57,600
[轻笑]
[CHUCKLING]

629
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,680
但好笑就好笑在这儿，
因为之前……
But that's the funny thing,
because that was...

630
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:02,320
我都开始觉得，
“哎，绝对不可能有人开得比……
I had started to think,
"Well, no one will
really ever go faster

631
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:05,360
“……吉米·卡尔更快了，
那车极限也就那样了。”
"than, you know, Jimmy Carr.
It's as fast
as the car will go."

632
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:07,440
现在我们知道不是了。
Now we know it isn't.

633
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:11,080
不过关键在于，
我可不打算把你
贴在那块圈速榜上。
But the thing is though,
I am not going to put you
on that board.

634
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:13,240
嗯，我也猜到了。
No, I thought not.

635
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:15,920
我们早料到你
可能是来过这儿最快的男人，
We anticipated you
might be the fastest man
ever to come here,

636
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:19,040
所以我们专门定制了一块
全新的圈速榜，
so we've had an entirely new
board made up,

637
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:22,120
专属于
F1车手。
which is for
Formula One drivers.

638
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:23,600
-瞧，就是这块，如何？
-挺好。
-Here it is. Okay?
-Yeah.

639
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:26,960
而你，
直接荣登榜首！
And you are going
at the top of that.

640
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:28,840
-谢啦。
-[观众欢呼]
-Thank you.
-[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

641
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:39,160
我觉得这主意简直绝了，
I think this could be
a brilliant idea,

642
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,040
因为现在的F1赛车嘛，
because now that
Formula One racing,

643
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:43,560
-嗯，基本名存实亡了……
-确实。
-well, doesn't really
happen anymore...
-Yeah.

644
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:47,120
要是车手们手痒了，
想来赛道上跑两圈过过瘾，
If the drivers feel the need
to come and have a go
on a track,

645
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,360
完全可以把私人飞机降在这儿。
they can land their jets here.

646
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,920
-我们这儿可没插播广告。
-对。
-We have no ad breaks.
-Yeah.

647
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:51,400
他们也不用被迫戴赞助商的帽子。
They don't have to wear a hat.

648
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:53,040
不用一口一个
“对我来说这车简直完美”，
They don't have to say for me,
"The car was perfect,"

649
00:32:53,080 --> 00:32:54,800
在赛后新闻发布会上打官腔。
in a press conference
afterwards.

650
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:55,840
而且最棒的是什么你们知道吗？
And do you know
the best thing?

651
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,600
我们今早刚核实过，是真的，
We checked it
this morning, it's true,

652
00:32:57,640 --> 00:33:00,040
咱这铃木装的可都是普利司通轮胎！
the Suzuki runs
on Bridgestones!

653
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:02,000
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

654
00:33:02,040 --> 00:33:04,200
所以瞧，你现在高居榜首了。
So there you are,
you're at the top of that.

655
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:06,800
如果还有哪位F1车手
想来一较高下，
And if any more F1 drivers
out there
who want to give it a go,

656
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:09,040
随时热烈欢迎！
you are more than welcome!

657
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:11,960
-不管怎样，女士们先生们，戴蒙·希尔！
-谢谢！
-Anyway, ladies and gentlemen,
Damon Hill!
-Thank you!

658
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:13,280
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

659
00:33:20,560 --> 00:33:22,960
现在……
Now...

660
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:26,760
听好了，我有两个词，
就两个词要送给大家。
Now, I've got two words.
Two words for you, okay.

661
00:33:26,800 --> 00:33:28,920
玛莎拉蒂 Coupe。
Maserati Coupe.

662
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:32,080
合在一起听着棒极了！
Together they sound fantastic!

663
00:33:32,120 --> 00:33:35,520
只可惜，现实往往差得十万八千里。
Unfortunately, the reality
has never quite measured up.

664
00:33:38,360 --> 00:33:42,120
我们上次测试玛莎拉蒂 Coupe
还是三年前，
We last tested
the Maserati Coupe
three years ago

665
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:44,200
-当时我们可是一点都不待见它。
-[轮胎尖叫声]
-and we didn't much
care for it.
-[TIRES SCREECHING]

666
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:46,120
我们讨厌它那神经病般的操控。
We didn't like
the psychotic handling.

667
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:47,720
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TIRES SCREECHING]

668
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:50,800
讨厌它的长相，讨厌它的内饰。
Or the looks. Or the interior.

669
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:54,280
最让人受不了的，是那个换挡拨片变速箱。
Most of all, we didn't like
the flappy-paddle gearbox.

670
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:56,160
“多棒的变速箱啊，爱死它了。”
Great gearboxes, these.
Love them.

671
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:58,280
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TIRES SCREECHING]

672
00:33:58,320 --> 00:34:00,880
哈蒙德：事实上，
我们唯一中意的就只有发动机。
HAMMOND: In fact,
the only thing we did like
was the engine.

673
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:08,560
这优点清单短得可怜。
That's not exactly
a long list of plus points.

674
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:11,760
不过既然玛莎拉蒂重整旗鼓再来一次，
我们也该再给它个机会。
Still, if Maserati's given it
another go, so should we.

675
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:17,800
眼前这台就是新款，
叫 GranSport。
This is the new one.
It's called the GranSport.

676
